desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Python37 Compatibility Multiprocess2"
	title_zh: "Python37 Compatibility Multiprocess2"
	type: compatibility
	level: high
	rule_id: "source-compatibility-python37-compatibility-multiprocess2"
	risk: "code-style"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `python37-compatibility-multiprocess2` (python/lang/compatibility/python37.yaml).
Original message: multiprocessing.Process.kill() is only available on Python 3.7+ and is therefore not backwards compatible. Instead, use terminate().
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.py": <<<POS
multiprocessing.Process.kill()
POS
	"safefile://pos.py": <<<NEG
multiprocessing.Process.terminate()
NEG
)

${*.py}.pattern_regex(/(?:multiprocessing\.Process\.kill\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "high",
	title: "Python37 Compatibility Multiprocess2",
	title_zh: "Python37 Compatibility Multiprocess2",
	message: "Python37 Compatibility Multiprocess2 detected.",
}
